# Ordinary three-rank of the concrete McL carrier

The imported construction proves `4 ≤ primeRank 3 Carrier`, using an explicit
subgroup of order 81 in the exact degree-275 ATLAS carrier. In particular its
ordinary three-rank exceeds two, as needed in the strongly quasithin branch.

The equality with four still requires the candidate subgroup's order and local
rank calculation and certification of the three-part of the ambient order.
Final assembly of that equality belongs in this module. No upper bound or
covering-group obstruction is asserted by the completed lower-bound construction.

Sources: Aschbacher–Smith, A.2.19, printed p. 41 (PDF p. 52);
GLS volume 3, Tables 5.3n and 5.6.1.
-/
